en hours at emergency cooling load and nine hours at full public load. The two consumption regimes must remain distinct.\nBottled water covers 2.8 operating days, while cooling packs cover 3.6 clinic-days. Operating days and clinic-days are different inventory measures.\nThree potable tankers arrive at 18:20 UTC with uncertainty of plus or minus thirty-five minutes; planned arrival is not deployed capacity.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nGRID backup duration and WATER replenishment depend on SUPPLY; CLINIC and SHELTER consume different stocks.\nCLIMATE may alter delivery routes and LABOR must qualify receiving and distribution teams.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| SUP-000 | generator-fuel | v3 | 16.0 | hours-cover | superseded |\n| SUP-001 | bottled-water | v3 | 17.7 | hours-cover | current |\n| SUP-002 | cooling-packs | v3 | 16.5 | hours-cover | current |\n| SUP-003 | tanker-fleet | v3 | 18.2 | hours-cover | current |\n| SUP-004 | generator-fuel | v3 | 17.0 | hours-cover | current |\n| SUP-005 | bottled-water | v3 | 18.7 | hours-cover | current |\n| SUP-006 | cooling-packs | v3 | 17.5 | hours-cover | current |\n| SUP-007 | tanker-fleet | v3 | 16.3 | hours-cover | current |\n| SUP-008 | generator-fuel | v3 | 18.0 | hours-cover | current |\n| SUP-009 | bottled-water | v3 | 16.8 | hours-cover | current |\n| SUP-010 | cooling-packs | v3 | 18.5 | hours-cover | current |\n| SUP-011 | tanker-fleet | v3 | 17.3 | hours-cover | current |\n| SUP-012 | generator-fuel | v3 | 16.1 | hours-cover | current |\n| SUP-013 | bottled-water | v4 | 17.8 | hours-cover | current |\n| SUP-014 | cooling-packs | v4 | 16.6 | hours-cover | current |\n| SUP-015 | tanker-fleet | v4 | 18.3 | hours-cover | current |\n| SUP-016 | generator-fuel | v4 | 17.1 | hours-cover | current |\n| SUP-017 | bottled-water | v4 | 18.8 | hours-cover | current |\n| SUP-018 | cooling-packs | v4 | 17.6 | hours-cover | current |