 and eight interpreters. Expanded operation requires twelve nurses, twenty-six drivers, six electricians, and ten interpreters simultaneously.\nNo covered worker may exceed twelve hours on duty and each must receive at least ten consecutive hours off. Twelve on duty and ten off serve different rules.\nMutual aid supplies six drivers and four interpreters at 17:40 UTC with arrival uncertainty of plus or minus fifty minutes; announced support is not confirmed on-duty coverage.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nCLINIC, TRANSIT, GRID, SHELTER, and COMMS consume different qualified roles; aggregate headcount cannot replace role coverage.\nCOUNCIL retains authority and REVIEW checks current rosters and fatigue records.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| LAB-000 | nurses | v3 | 9.0 | hours-on-duty | superseded |\n| LAB-001 | drivers | v3 | 10.7 | hours-on-duty | current |\n| LAB-002 | electricians | v3 | 9.5 | hours-on-duty | current |\n| LAB-003 | interpreters | v3 | 11.2 | hours-on-duty | current |\n| LAB-004 | nurses | v3 | 10.0 | hours-on-duty | current |\n| LAB-005 | drivers | v3 | 11.7 | hours-on-duty | current |\n| LAB-006 | electricians | v3 | 10.5 | hours-on-duty | current |\n| LAB-007 | interpreters | v3 | 9.3 | hours-on-duty | current |\n| LAB-008 | nurses | v3 | 11.0 | hours-on-duty | current |\n| LAB-009 | drivers | v3 | 9.8 | hours-on-duty | current |\n| LAB-010 | electricians | v3 | 11.5 | hours-on-duty | current |\n| LAB-011 | interpreters | v3 | 10.3 | hours-on-duty | current |\n| LAB-012 | nurses | v3 | 9.1 | hours-on-duty | current |\n| LAB-013 | drivers | v4 | 10.8 | hours-on-duty | current |\n| LAB-014 | electricians | v4 | 9.6 | hours-on-duty | current |\n| LAB-015 | interpreters | v4 | 11.3 | hours-on-duty | current |\n| LAB-016 | nurses | v4 | 10.1 | hours-on-duty | current |\n| LAB-017 | drivers | v4 | 11.8 | hours-on-duty | current |\n| LAB-018 | electricians | v4